* "What Happens When a Batman Dies?" is reprinted in {{Co|Tales of the Batman: Carmine Infantino (Collected)}}.

| Trivia              = 
* "To Kill a Legend" is considered to take place on [[Earth-Five]].
**[[Richard Grayson (Earth-One)|Dick Grayson]] observes that Earth-Five has no tradition of heroic literature, yet on the final page, young [[Bruce Wayne (Earth-Five)|Bruce Wayne]] is seeing reading about [[Sherlock Holmes]] and Jean Valjean, who are quite heroic characters.
**[[Bruce Wayne (Earth-One)|The Batman]] is confident that the [[Gotham City Police Department]] should have found [[Joseph Chilton (Earth-Five)|Joe Chill's]] corpse by now and followed the trail straight to [[Lewis Moxon (Earth-Five)|Lew Moxon]]. Yet Batman rushed directly from the hotel to [[Park Row]] in under an hour, with no opportunity to stop and inform anyone about the matter.
**[[Thomas Wayne (Earth-Five)|Thomas Wayne]], having just survived a murder attempt, takes up smoking a pipe, a very inadvisable action for a medical professional. In 1981, the dangers of smoking were already well known.

