| Notes               = 
* This story is reprinted in:
** {{co|Batman: Year One (Collected)}}
** {{co|DC Finest: Batman: Year One & Two (Collected)}}
* The flashback scenes from this issue take place with scenes shown in the issue {{c|Batman: Legends of the Dark Knight #1}}.
* This issue establishes that [[Bruce Wayne (New Earth)|Bruce Wayne]] is twenty-five years old when he arrives in Gotham on January 4 and begins his career as Batman in early April when he is twenty-six (due to his February 19 birthday, which comes from a Pre-Crisis source but has never been contradicted). He furthermore says his parents were killed eighteen years ago, making him eight at the time, which is supported by sources including the [[Zero Hour]] timeline and {{c|Superman/Batman Secret Files & Origins 2003}}.
* It is briefly stated in this issue that [[James Gordon (New Earth)|James Gordon]] was forced to leave [[Chicago]] after an incident involving other corrupt police officers. This incident is expanded upon in the ''[[Batman: Gordon of Gotham Vol 1|Gordon of Gotham]]'' limited series. 
* The title of the story references the first Batman origin story "Who He Is and How He Came To Be," first published in {{c|Detective Comics #33}}. Several sequences in this issue mirror that story.
* This issue was directly adapted into the ''[[DC High Volume: Batman (Podcast)|DC High Volume: Batman]]'' episode "[[DC High Volume: Batman (Podcast) Episode: Year One - Chapter 1|Year One - Chapter 1]]".
| Trivia              = * Bruce Wayne references several Gotham City landmarks, namely [[Robinson Park]], the Finger Memorial and the Sprang Mission. These locales are named after creators [[Jerry Robinson]], [[Bill Finger]] and [[Dick Sprang]]. 
