| Quotation           = [[Sarah Essen (New Earth)|Sgt. Essen]] informed me that [[Bruce Wayne (New Earth)|Wayne]]'s [[Wayne Family|parents]] were murdered by a [[Joseph Chilton (New Earth)|mugger]] when he was eight years old. That's enough motive, I suppose, to make a man dress like [[Dracula]] and assault criminals...
| Speaker             = [[James Gordon (New Earth)|Lt. Gordon]]

| StoryTitle1         = [[Batman: Year One|Year One]], Chapter Three: Black Dawn

| Synopsis1           = Flaming piles of debris drop down on top of Batman as the [[Gotham City]] SWAT team fires a firebomb at the derelict apartment building. Flammable materials within his utility belt begin to explode. [[Bruce Wayne (New Earth)|Batman]] finds an electrical cover and uses it to mask his presence. [[File:Batman 0397.jpg|thumb|left|250px|[[Bruce Wayne (New Earth)|Batman]] vs. the [[Gotham City Police Department|GCPD]]]] A ground crew enters the building and begins sifting through the rubble. Batman lures them into a lower section of the building and traps them. 

Before preparing his escape, Batman uses a remote device to signal a massive flock of bats from the Batcave. The swarm of bats descends on the area, giving Batman a chance to use them for cover to mask his escape. Several police squad cars attempt to follow the bat swarm, with one even driving off Gotham Pier. Dozens of bystanders (including [[Selina Kyle (New Earth)|Selina Kyle]]) are forced to get rabies vaccinations. 

[[File:Catwoman 0144.jpg|thumb|right|200px|[[Selina Kyle (New Earth)|Selina Kyle]] becomes [[Catwoman]]]]
Later, [[James Gordon (New Earth)|Jim Gordon]] consults with [[Sarah Essen (New Earth)|Sarah Essen]] over the Batman issue. Sarah suspects that Batman may, in fact, be Bruce Wayne. Wayne has an alibi, however, citing that he was skiing in Switzerland during the recent incident.

Gordon walks Essen home, and the two share a romantic embrace. Jim instantly feels guilty knowing that his pregnant wife is home waiting for him.

In Gotham's East End, Selina Kyle decides to go into a different line of work. She punches out her pimp, Stan, and takes [[Holly Robinson (New Earth)|Holly]] with her. She fashions a costume for herself and becomes Catwoman for the first time. 

