| Synopsis1           = ''' Below '''

Bruce is once again in Hell, below everything. And once again, his father, Brian Banner, greets him, welcoming him home. Every time he dies, he comes back here for a while, then he comes back. They all do, all the gamma people. It is how it works: the third form of gamma, a divine essence. The energy of the Creator's counterpart.
Bruce refuses to believe this, but Brian tells him that, of all people, he should understand that there could be a middle ground. Still, Bruce is convinced of one thing: if there is one man that deserves the fate of being alone in Hell, that is Brian.
But Bruce's father tells him he is not always alone: that is when Bruce sees his mother, her back turned to face him. He cries and shouts, telling her to at least turn to look at him. In that moment, the [[Green Door]] opens, and Bruce is back... inside.

The Immortal Hulk is out to protect him now.
The Hulk and the Red Harpy both fight the Abomination, and the Hulk tells the Red Harpy to remove the stomach from their opponent, as his acid is able to shut down their gamma healing factor. Jackie, shocked about the fact that Betty literally ate the Hulk's heart moments before, needs an explanation, and the Hulk provides it: Betty gave him a "hard reset" so that he could recover and get back to business as quickly as possible. Jackie wanted a slice of the Hulk's world, and here it is. But in that moment, one of Shadow Base's War Wagons attacks, followed by another one.

Betty and the Hulk once again coordinate themselves, and succeed in smashing and blowing up both tanks, while also taking care of a re-energized Abomination. As General [[Reginald Fortean (Earth-616)|Reginald Fortean]] watches another plan crumble, Jackie asks the Hulk if the theory developed by Amadeus Cho, telling that Bruce is subconsciously keeping his other side in check about killing people, is true. The Immortal Hulk answers that for the other Hulks, it probably is.
They recover the body of Rick Jones from the insides of the Abomination and leave, with Shadow Base's remaining forces doing the same, as Gamma Flight is approaching.
As always, they are late, but Samson notices the Red Harpy on a roof, going away.

''' The End of Times '''

"Can you hear me?" speaks a mysterious voice, addressing Bruce Banner. A rock floats in space, Banner standing on it with a corpse at his side. A bright light, enveloping an angelic being, gets closer and closer to him. He asks Bruce if he knows who speaks to him. If Bruce knows who he himself is. It is time to make his choice, to decide if he is of Geburah or Golachab. Man or monster.
"What will Bruce Banner become?" asks the voice.

