| Synopsis1           = Following the dissolution of his company, Peter lands on some hard times as [[Peter Parker (Earth-616)|Spider-Man]] due to [[Wilson Fisk (Earth-616)|Kingpin]] winning the Mayorship for his protecting New Yorkers during [[Hydra (Earth-616)|Hydra's]] [[Secret Empire (Event)|usurpation]], Fisk has been pretending to be Spidey's biggest supporter and managed to put the web-head at odds against the whole superhero community. Trying to see a positive in his personal life, Peter Parker enjoys his job as a science editor at the [[Daily Bugle (The DB!) (Earth-616)|Daily Bugle]] until he is accused by [[Cindy Lawton (Earth-616)|Cindy Lawton]] of plagiarizing his doctoral thesis from that of [[Otto Octavius]] (who occupied his body at that time.) As this was proven by an advanced computer comparison algorithm. the exposure results in Peter losing his job. He later fights with [[Maybelle Parker (Earth-616)|Aunt May]] over his hiding from the fallout of his company and the loss of his doctorate.

Trying to think of what to do next, he ventures as Spider-Man he manages to thwart an alien invasion upon discovering that it was all a trick of [[Quentin Beck (Earth-616)|Mysterio]]. Realizing a monotony of the encounter, Spider-Man webs Mysterio to a building for authorities to take into custody. As Peter, he apologizes for everything from his body swap with Otto to his recent attack by [[Norman Osborn (Earth-616)|Red Goblin]], and makes amends with [[Mary Jane Watson (Earth-616)|Mary Jane Watson]]. Reconciled, the two begin dating again and find some measure of glee.

