| Quotation           = [[Marko (Saga)|You're]] not the only one who's found [[Alana (Saga)|someone new]], all right? The [[Billy (Saga)|man]] I '''love''' has been hurt, and I need your help to make him whole again.
| Speaker             = [[Gwendolyn (Saga)|Gwendolyn]]

| StoryTitle1         = 
| Synopsis1           = [[Lying Cat (Saga)|Lying Cat]] tackles [[Klara (Saga)|Klara]], who manages to stab Lying Cat in the eye with her finger before being knocked unconscious. [[Izabel (Saga)|Izabel]] appears, and tells Lying Cat to stand down, as it was against the ordinance of Lying Cats to break the rules, and that he and ([[Gwendolyn (Saga)|Gwendolyn]]) have no right to execute civilians in their own home, like they did [[D. Oswald Heist (Saga)|D. Oswald Heist]]. Izabel then uses her illusion ability to scare Lying Cat out of D. Oswald Heist's home. She doesn't notice [[Prince Robot IV (Saga)|Prince Robot IV]] has also entered the house. 

On the rooftop, [[Marko (Saga)|Marko]] and [[Alana (Saga)|Alana]] try to decide what to do next, and if they should jump. Alana reminds Marko that her wings are vestigial, and don't work. [[Gwendolyn (Saga)|Gwendolyn]] bursts onto the rooftop, and demands to know the ingredient needed for a long-term healing spell for the man she admits to having fallen in love with ([[Billy (Saga)|The Will]]).

Below, a fire has been ignited, and it is revealed that [[Prince Robot IV (Saga)|Prince Robot IV's]] mind has been rebooted. Prince Robot IV asks Izabel for commands, and she orders him to take the unconscious Klara outside. Prince Robot IV complies, and is then asked by Izabel to complete another task which prompts Prince Robot IV say that he needs to get back to his ship, and to ask Izabel for her name and rank. This prompts Izabel to let Prince Robot IV go on about his own business.

Back on the rooftop, Alana attempts to tell Gwendolyn about a nearby hospital on [[Landfall]]. The two women end up in an argument over Marko, and Gwendolyn uses The Will's lance to attempt to kill Alana. Marko pushes Alana and [[Hazel (Saga)|Hazel]] off the roof. This shocks Gwendolyn, and as Marko begins telling Gwendolyn the reason for their breakup, she cuts him off, and tells him he broke her heart. Alana suddenly appears, using her wings to fly, and shoots Gwendolyn with the [[Heartbreaker]], knocking her out.

On [[Jetsam]], [[Upsher (Saga)|Upsher]] and [[Doff (Saga)|Doff]] receive information from their chief about a chance to work on a story about Prince Robot IV, who has been missing for weeks, and is about to have his first baby with his [[Princess Robot (Saga)|wife]]. Upsher and Doff turn the story down as they still have the poison from [[The Brand (Saga)|The Brand]] in their systems.

In a hospital on Landfall, The Will lies in a semi-conscious state in the intensive care unit. The Brand visits The Will, informing the hospital staff she is his sister. Upon The Brand's arrival, The Will utters the name "Sophie."

Elsewhere, a few months later, Alana and her family have moved forward in their lives, and Hazel has begun walking.

